  "circulation": "Parallel boardwalks and two crossings keep every required building connected without entering water. A broad graded entrance rises to the +1.2 m decks. Ferry stage is reachable scenery, not extraction transport; return remains to the land-based van.",
  "systems": "Flooded lower warehouse floor is visible below the dry route and excluded from navigation. Water reflection, insects, pumps and timber creak have ordinary sources; fog cannot hide all route markers.",
  "campaign": "Property deeds describe homes lost to water; the actual reachable homes remain fixed. Reclaimed settlement contracts may revisit records without requiring a simulated receding tide.",
  "refine": [
    "Replace long boardwalk envelopes with measured supports, continuous deck meshes and invariant rails; ensure 2 m clear width.",
    "Define flood plane and collision once per mission; no required wading, swimming or leap.",
    "The entrance rise needs a real supported ramp and level intermediate landings."
  ],
